      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Historic Lumberland Town Hall, originally the 1879 Glen Spey School, now hosts a museum room and cultural events.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/glen_spey_new_york",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Glen Spey’s landscape includes Mohican Lake, a 180‑acre reservoir with 8 miles of shoreline popular for fishing and hiking.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/glen_spey_new_york",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The area was originally inhabited by the Lenape, who used the river for hunting and fishing as early as 12,000 years ago.",
